</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, this paper proposes OD-LLM, a principled and efficient compression framework designed to enable large language models to operate effectively within the constraints of on-device recommendation systems.
By integrating token-level normalization, low-rank decomposition, and progressive alignment into a unified architecture, OD-LLM delivers substantially smaller models that preserve the nuanced sequential patterns essential to high-quality sequential recommendations.
Unlike conventional compression methods, OD-LLM is tailored to the behavioral sensitivity and temporal dependencies characteristic to user–item interactions, offering both theoretical rigor and practical viability. Unlike general model compression techniques, our method is much fast for both compression and inference and can be flexibly applied to diffferent LLMs.
Our findings demonstrate that it is possible to retain the expressive power of LLMs for the strict resource demands of edge environments – a significant step toward privacy-preserving, real-time personalized sequential recommendation on local devices.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
